===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{senseid|en|geometry}}{{lb|en|geometry}} A [[polyhedron]] with [[parallel#Adjective|parallel]] [[end#Noun|ends]] of the [[same#Adjective|same]] [[polygonal]] [[shape#Noun|shape]] and [[size#Noun|size]], the other [[face#Noun|faces]] being [[parallelogram]]-[[shaped#Adjective|shaped]] [[sides]].
## An [[object#Noun|object]] having the [[shape#Noun|shape]] of a [[geometrical]] prism ''({{senseno|en|geometry}})''.
## {{lb|en|construction}} A {{l|en|cutting|t=[[open#Adjective|open]] [[passage#Noun|passage]] at a [[level#Noun|level]] [[low#Adjective|lower]] than the [[surrounding#Adjective|surrounding]] [[terrain]], [[dig#Verb|dug]] for a [[canal#Noun|canal]], [[railway]], or [[road#Noun|road]] to [[go through]]}} or an [[embankment]] [[shape#Verb|shaped]] like a prism ''({{senseno|en|geometry}})'' or a [[number#Noun|number]] of prisms, such that its [[volume#Noun|volume]] can be [[easily]] [[calculate]]d.
## {{senseid|en|crystal}}{{lb|en|crystallography}} A [[crystal#Noun|crystal]] in which the faces are parallel to the [[vertical#Adjective|vertical]] [[axis]].
## {{senseid|en|optics}}{{lb|en|optics}} A [[transparent]] [[block#Noun|block]] in the shape of a prism ''({{senseno|en|geometry}})'', [[typically]] with [[triangular]] ends, [[use#Verb|used]] to [[reflect]] or [[refract]] [[light#Noun|light]].
##* {{RQ:Newton Opticks|book=1|chapter=Prop[osition] I. Theor[y] I. Lights which Differ in Colour, Differ also in Degrees of Refrangibility.|pages=13 and 17|pageref=13|passage=&#91;[https://archive.org/details/opticksortreatis00newt/page/n22/mode/1up page 13]&#93; One of theſe Parts [of a piece of black paper] I painted vvith a red Colour and the other vvith a blevv. {{...}} This Paper I vievved through a '''Priſm''' of ſolid Glaſs, vvhoſe tvvo Sides through vvhich the Light paſſed to the Eye vvere plane and vvell poliſhed, and contained an Angle of about Sixty Degrees: vvhich Angle I call the refracting Angle of the '''Priſm'''. {{...}} &#91;[https://archive.org/details/opticksortreatis00newt/page/n26/mode/1up page 17]&#93; Theſe Experiments may ſuffice for the Colours of Natural Bodies. For in the Colours made by the Refraction of '''Priſms''' this Propoſition vvill appear by the Experiments vvhich are novv to follovv in the next Propoſition.}}
##* {{RQ:Thomson Spring|lines=207–211|page=10|passage=Here, avvful [[w:Isaac Newton|[Isaac] {{smallcaps|Newton}}]], the diſſolving clouds / Form, fronting on the ſun, thy ſhovvery '''priſm'''; / And to the ſage-inſtructed eye unfold / The various tvvine of light, by thee diſclos'd / From the vvhite mingling maze.}}
### {{lb|en|archaic}} A [[spectrum]] [[produce#Verb|produced]] by light being refracted through a prism.
###* {{RQ:Tennyson Poems 1842|volume=II|poem=The Day-Dream|page=151|passage=The beams, that thro' the Oriel shine, / Make '''prisms''' in every carven glass, {{...}}}}
# {{senseid|en|surveying}}{{lb|en|by extension|surveying}} A {{l|en|retroreflector|t=[[device]] which reflects light back to its [[source#Noun|source]] with [[minimum#Adjective|minimum]] [[scattering#Noun|scattering]]}} which is usually [[attach]]ed to a [[surveying#Noun|surveying]] [[pole#Noun|pole]] as a [[target#Noun|target]] for a [[total station]] which [[emit]]s a light [[beam#Noun|beam]] at the device and calculates how [[long#Adjective|long]] it [[take#Verb|takes]] to be reflected back in order to [[measure#Verb|measure]] [[distance#Noun|distance]].
# {{lb|en|figurative}} A [[perspective]] that [[color#Verb|colours]] one's [[perception]].
#* {{RQ:Irving Sketch Book|title=Stratford-on-Avon|page=87|passage=I had surveyed the landscape through the '''prism''' of poetry, which tinged every object with the hues of the rainbow.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|author=w:Phil McNulty|title=[[w:Manchester City F.C.|Manchester City]] 1 – 0 {{w|Inter Milan}}|work=w:BBC Sport|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20240410053021/https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/65845807|date=10 June 2023|passage=It is a simple fact that many outside the Abu Dhabi-owned club will always view their triumph through the '''prism''' of the charges of 115 financial breaches brought against them by the Premier League, charges they fiercely deny.}}

